  ```yaml
  handle:
    class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.CityAtCapacityHandler
  ```

### 2. Function classes that count owners by city / enforce the 50 limit

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckCityCapacity.java` (full content):
```java
public class CheckCityCapacity {
    static final int CAPACITY = 50;

    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws CityAtCapacityException {
        String city = normalize(owner.getCity());
        long count = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
                .filter(other -> !other.getId().equals(owner.getId()))
                .filter(other -> city.equals(normalize(other.getCity())))
                .count();
        if (count >= CAPACITY) {
            throw new CityAtCapacityException(owner.getCity());
        }
    }

    static String normalize(String value) {
        return value == null ? "" : value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
    }
}
```
This throws a 409 (see handler below). It counts via `ownerRepository.findAll()` streamed and filtered by normalized city — there is no dedicated count-by-city repository method.

